    "sensitivity": {
      "payout_ratios": [
        "0.50",
        "0.85"
      ],
      "fade_years": [
        0,
        10
      ],
      "extra_cost_of_equity": "0.02",
      "no_franchise_tail": "Zero future earnings/distributions and no terminal liquidation recovery; extreme total-loss scenario, not an estimated probability or the routine bear price."
    },
    "rationale": {
      "income": "FY2025 parent profit fell 4.53%; H1 2026 fell 1.95%, and ex-nonrecurring profit fell 2.04%. The lower TTM anchor removes disclosed exceptional items but is not through-cycle normalized earnings. Five annual -5/0/+5 percent paths represent continued deterioration, stabilization, and an explicitly optimistic recovery, not analyst consensus. They are not calculated by compounding book equity at historical ROE.",
      "price_event": "July's SKU/channel price increases are one-time level changes. Channel weights, volumes and margins are uncertain; no additional whole-company price uplift is stacked onto the profit paths.",
      "payout": "Annual report physical page 33 reports combined distribution including repurchases of 71,153,295,260.53 and repurchases of 6,120,088,960.04; the difference is proposed/interim cash dividends of 65,033,206,300.49, about 79% of annual parent profit. The 75% assumption is a research policy below that observation, not a future company commitment. H1 mother-company CFO 15,224,606,455.02 and capex 828,735,611.53 do not cover dividends/interest paid of 35,032,574,305.20; cash fell from 85,687,080,245.45 to 61,596,625,049.44. Opening cash and subsidiary remittances matter. Consolidated finance-company deposits cannot be treated as distributable cash.",
      "capital_and_fade": "Profit is projected independently for five years; retained earnings increase book capital without automatically earning historic franchise returns. Beginning-equity ROE then fades linearly to the scenario cost of equity over five years. The terminal regime earns its capital cost with growth funded by retention; it contains no perpetual excess franchise value. Five-year horizons are bounded research choices, tested with immediate and ten-year fade, not established forecasts.",
      "discount": "Use the archived CNY sovereign-yield plus listed-equity beta times China total ERP policy. Select central for base and upper/lower for bear/bull. Components are asynchronous dated proxies; the beta interval is not a forward cost-of-equity confidence interval. The +200bp sensitivity tests a materially higher required return; no second country premium is added.",
      "peer": "Wuliangye H1 growth is off restated revenue/profit comparatives; negative operating cash flow and higher sales-expense intensity counter an assumption of automatic industry recovery. Peer growth is not transferred to Moutai.",
      "time_bridge": "The June-30 book basis is a modelling origin using information available only by the actual registration/valuation timestamp. Annual cash-flow values are transported to that valuation timestamp with the matching discount convention; this is not observed September net assets and must never be backfilled into June decisions. June dividends/repurchases already reflected in book equity are not subtracted again."
    },
    "review_required_before_simulation_admission": [
      "Confirm current model facts, time bridge, payout/capital assumptions and sensitivity results are admissible for the stated paper scope.",
      "Bind the new model and policy to the P1 producer/consumer contracts and daily account; source truth and arithmetic alone do not grant simulation or live admission."
    ],
